<===> README.md
Bogus selectors (e.g. with two combinators in a row) are omitted from the
output like in dart-sass, also if the bogus part is not the first compound,
and leading combinators in selector pseudo-classes other than `:has()`.
(libsass only checked the first component).
<===>
================================================================================
<===> first_component/input.scss
.w > > .x .y {x: y}
<===> first_component/output.css

<===>
================================================================================
<===> has_leading/input.scss
:has(> .a) {x: y}
<===> has_leading/output.css
:has(> .a) {
  x: y;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> is_leading/input.scss
:is(> .a) {x: y}
<===> is_leading/output.css

<===>
================================================================================
<===> later_component/input.scss
a { .w .x > > .y {x: y} }
<===> later_component/output.css

<===>
================================================================================
<===> later_pseudo/input.scss
a .b :is(.c > > .d) {x: y}
<===> later_pseudo/output.css

<===>
================================================================================
<===> not_leading/input.scss
:not(> .a) {x: y}
<===> not_leading/output.css

<===>
================================================================================
<===> useless_pseudo/input.scss
.a :is(> .b) .c {x: y}
<===> useless_pseudo/output.css

